            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "China's COMAC falls behind on C919 aircraft delivery targets, filings show",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Chinese planemaker COMAC is falling behind on previously stated delivery targets for the production of its narrow-body C919 commercial plane, according to regulatory filings from the three airlines that fly the model.  China Eastern Airlines, Air China and China Southern were expecting 32 of the planes to be delivered this year, but as of September only five have been handed over from COMAC, according to airline financial reports and data from ch-aviation and Flightradar24.  The state-owned manufacturer has cut its own C919 production target to 25 this year from a previously stated goal of 75, Bloomberg reported on Wednesday, citing sources familiar with the matter.",
